    "updated_at": "2022-01-13T14:54:31Z",
    "body": "The most obvious way I can see to set this is:\r\n```pwsh\r\n$prompt = prompt\r\nSet-PSReadLineOption -ExtraPromptLineCount ($prompt.Split(\"`n\").Length - 1)\r\n```\r\n\r\nThe question is whether to do that once on startup or to save the prompt from `Invoke-Native` in the `global:prompt` function and set it on each call.\r\n\r\nAlso if there is anything faster than ``.Split(\"`n\")`` (Might be a premature optimization to consider this)",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "pin": null,
    "reactions": {
